        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-159616",
        ":question/problem": "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ given that $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}\\cdot (1)-y\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
