        ":question/problem": "Find ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ for $f(x,y)=8x{y}^{4}+\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The notation ${f}_{x}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8x{y}^{4}+\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(8x{y}^{4})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}\\right) \\\\  & =8{y}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)+3{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}\\left(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\right) \\\\  & =8{y}^{4}\\cdot 1+3{y}^{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\right) \\\\  & =8{y}^{4}-\\frac{12{y}^{2}}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
